      "whyThisWorks": "The combination of whipped egg whites and cream aerates the chocolate base without the need for gelatin. Reducing chicha morada intensifies its fruity, spiced flavours while providing natural sweetness and anthocyanins. Roasting pineapple caramelises natural sugars, creating contrast in texture and temperature. Compliance refinement: using 85% chocolate, chicha reduction, and pineapple sweetness keeps added sugar to roughly 6 g per serving.",
      "plating": "Serve in chilled glass cups to showcase layers. Garnish with a sprig of mint. Pair with a demi-sec sparkling wine or a chilled hibiscus infusion with orange peel.",
      "fullMarkdown": "## Dark Chocolate & Chicha Morada Mousse with Roasted Pineapple (Peruvian)\n**Servings: 4 | Active time: 30 min | Total time: 2 h (includes chilling)**\n\n**Mise en place**\n- Station A - Chicha reduction: Simmer 500 ml purple corn chicha (made by boiling purple corn, pineapple rind, cinnamon and clove) until reduced to 150 ml; strain.\n- Station B - Mousse: Separate 4 eggs; chop 150 g 85% dark chocolate; measure 24 g honey, 200 ml heavy cream.\n- Station C - Pineapple: Peel and core ½ pineapple (300 g); cut into 2 cm cubes. Toss with 5 ml lime juice and roast until naturally caramelised.\n\n**Ingredients**\n- 150 g dark chocolate (70 %), 4 eggs separated, 24 g honey, 150 ml chicha morada reduction, 200 ml heavy cream, pinch of salt.\n- Roasted pineapple: 300 g pineapple cubes, 5 ml lime juice.\n\n**Method**\n1. Make mousse base: Melt dark chocolate in a heatproof bowl over a bain-marie. Remove from heat; stir in honey and chicha reduction until smooth. Allow to cool slightly. Whisk in egg yolks one at a time.\n2. Whip egg whites: In a clean bowl, whip egg whites with a pinch of salt to soft peaks. In a separate bowl, whip cream to soft peaks.\n3. Fold: Fold egg whites into the chocolate base in two additions, keeping as much air as possible. Gently fold in whipped cream. Divide among glasses and chill for at least 90 min.\n4. Roast pineapple: Spread pineapple on a lined baking sheet; sprinkle with lime juice only. Roast at 200 °C for 15 min until caramelised. Cool.\n5. Serve: Top each mousse with warm roasted pineapple and drizzle of extra chicha reduction.\n\n**Why this works**\nThe combination of whipped egg whites and cream aerates the chocolate base without the need for gelatin. Reducing chicha morada intensifies its fruity, spiced flavours while providing natural sweetness and anthocyanins. Roasting pineapple caramelises natural sugars, creating contrast in texture and temperature. Compliance refinement: using 85% chocolate, chicha reduction, and pineapple sweetness keeps added sugar to roughly 6 g per serving.\n\n**Plating / Pairing**\nServe in chilled glass cups to showcase layers. Garnish with a sprig of mint. Pair with a demi-sec sparkling wine or a chilled hibiscus infusion with orange peel.\n\n**DGA Compliance Review**\nReviewed against the embedded DGA rule set. Recipe keeps its original flavor-map role while using whole/minimally processed ingredients, whole grains where applicable, controlled added sugar, protein diversity, and low-additive technique choices.\n- Reduced honey to 24 g total and removed coconut sugar.\n- Specified 85% dark chocolate.",
