      "fullMarkdown": "## Elote-Style Corn Ribs (Mexican)\n**Servings: 4 | Active time: 20 min | Total time: 40 min**\n\n**Mise en place**\n- Station A - Corn: Quarter 4 ears of corn lengthwise to form “ribs.”\n- Station B - Seasoning: Mix 30 ml olive oil, 10 g smoked paprika, 5 g cumin, 5 g chili powder, 5 g garlic powder and 5 g salt.\n- Station C - Sauce & toppings: Blend 130 g Greek yoghurt with 20 g homemade olive-oil aioli, 1 chipotle chile, 10 ml lime juice and 20 g cilantro; crumble 50 g cotija cheese; chop extra cilantro.\n\n**Ingredients**\n- 4 ears corn, 30 ml olive oil, 10 g smoked paprika, 5 g cumin, 5 g chili powder, 5 g garlic powder, 5 g salt.\n- Sauce: 130 g Greek yoghurt, 20 g homemade olive-oil aioli, 1 chipotle chile, 10 ml lime juice, 20 g cilantro.\n- Garnish: 50 g cotija cheese, extra cilantro, lime wedges.\n\n**Method**\n1. Season corn: Toss corn ribs with spice oil mixture until well coated.\n2. Roast or grill: Arrange on a baking sheet and roast at 220 °C for 20 min, turning once, until kernels char and curl slightly. Alternatively, grill over medium-high heat.\n3. Prepare sauce: Blend yoghurt, homemade aioli, chipotle, lime juice and cilantro until smooth; season to taste.\n4. Serve: Drizzle corn ribs with sauce, sprinkle with cotija and cilantro, and serve with lime wedges.\n\n**Why this works**\nCutting corn into ribs increases surface area for caramelisation and creates a fun, handheld snack. Roasting at high heat develops charred, sweet notes without deep frying. The yoghurt-mayo sauce provides creaminess while chipotle adds smoky heat. Compliance refinement: homemade aioli and unsweetened yoghurt avoid commercial emulsified condiment additives while maintaining creamy elote richness.\n\n**Plating / Pairing**\nServe on a board lined with parchment. Pair with a light lager or agua de tamarindo.\n\n**DGA Compliance Review**\nReviewed against the embedded DGA rule set. Recipe keeps its original flavor-map role while using whole/minimally processed ingredients, whole grains where applicable, controlled added sugar, protein diversity, and low-additive technique choices.\n- Replaced commercial emulsified condiment with yoghurt plus homemade olive-oil aioli.",
