      "whyThisWorks": "Using almond meal and whole-wheat breadcrumbs reduces refined grains and increases healthy fats. Baking rather than shallow-frying delivers a crisp crust with less oil. Aji verde provides a tangy herbal counterpoint to the rich tomato and melted cheese. Compliance refinement: grated carrot replaces most added sugar in the tomato sauce while preserving sweetness and body.",
      "plating": "Serve on wide plates with salad spread underneath. Pair with a medium-bodied red like Sangiovese or a lime-mint sparkling water.",
      "fullMarkdown": "## Grilled Chicken Parmigiana with Aji Verde & Quinoa Salad (Italian × Peruvian)\n**Servings: 4 | Active time: 45 min | Total time: 1 h 15 min**\n\n**Mise en place**\n- Station A - Chicken: Pound 4 free-range chicken breasts (150 g each) to 1 cm thickness. Prepare breading station: 100 g almond meal mixed with 50 g whole-wheat breadcrumbs and 10 g grated Parmesan; beat 2 eggs; measure 50 g flour seasoned with salt and pepper.\n- Station B - Sauce: Simmer 500 g crushed San Marzano tomatoes with 2 minced garlic cloves, 5 ml olive oil, 5 g dried oregano, and 1 small grated carrot or 2 g honey only if tomatoes taste sharp until thickened.\n- Station C - Aji verde: Blend 50 g cilantro, 1 jalapeño, 1 garlic clove, 30 ml lime juice, 50 g Greek yoghurt, 30 ml olive oil and 5 g salt until smooth.\n- Station D - Quinoa salad: Cook 200 g quinoa in 400 ml water; dice 1 cucumber, 1 bell pepper, 1 avocado; chop 20 g mint.\n\n**Ingredients**\n- 4 chicken breasts (600 g total), 50 g flour, 2 eggs, 100 g almond meal, 50 g whole-wheat breadcrumbs, 10 g Parmesan, 500 g crushed tomatoes, garlic, oregano, sugar, 150 g fresh mozzarella, olive oil.\n- Aji verde: 50 g cilantro, 1 jalapeño, 1 garlic clove, 30 ml lime juice, 50 g Greek yoghurt, 30 ml olive oil, salt.\n- Quinoa salad: 200 g quinoa, 1 cucumber, 1 bell pepper, 1 avocado, 20 g mint, 30 ml lemon juice, 15 ml olive oil.\n\n**Method**\n1. Prepare sauce: Simmer tomatoes with garlic, oregano and grated carrot for 20 min until rich and naturally sweet; season with salt and pepper.\n2. Bread chicken: Dredge pounded chicken in flour, dip in egg, then coat with almond-breadcrumb mixture. Drizzle with olive oil.\n3. Bake or air-fry: Arrange breaded chicken on a rack and bake at 200 °C for 15 min or air-fry until crisp and cooked through. Top each cutlet with spoonful of tomato sauce and slice of mozzarella; return to oven for 5 min to melt.\n4. Make aji verde: Blend all sauce ingredients until smooth and vibrant green.\n5. Quinoa salad: Fluff cooked quinoa and toss with diced cucumber, bell pepper, avocado, mint, lemon juice and olive oil; season.\n6. Serve: Plate chicken parmigiana on quinoa salad; drizzle with aji verde.\n\n**Why this works**\nUsing almond meal and whole-wheat breadcrumbs reduces refined grains and increases healthy fats. Baking rather than shallow-frying delivers a crisp crust with less oil. Aji verde provides a tangy herbal counterpoint to the rich tomato and melted cheese. Compliance refinement: grated carrot replaces most added sugar in the tomato sauce while preserving sweetness and body.\n\n**Plating / Pairing**\nServe on wide plates with salad spread underneath. Pair with a medium-bodied red like Sangiovese or a lime-mint sparkling water.\n\n**DGA Compliance Review**\nReviewed against the embedded DGA rule set. Recipe keeps its original flavor-map role while using whole/minimally processed ingredients, whole grains where applicable, controlled added sugar, protein diversity, and low-additive technique choices.\n- Replaced added sugar in tomato sauce with grated carrot, with 2 g honey only if needed.",
