      "fullMarkdown": "## Korean Bulgogi Breakfast Burrito (Korean × Mexican)\n**Servings: 4 | Active time: 35 min | Total time: 50 min**\n\n**Mise en place**\n- Station A - Bulgogi: Thinly slice 400 g beef sirloin and marinate with 25 ml low-sodium soy sauce, 6 g honey or 40 g grated pear, 10 ml sesame oil, 2 g grated ginger, 2 cloves minced garlic, 5 ml rice vinegar and 5 ml gochujang. Rest 20 min.\n- Station B - Rice & eggs: Cook 200 g brown rice; scramble 4 eggs with 30 ml milk and a pinch of salt.\n- Station C - Pickles & fillings: Thinly slice 1 cucumber, toss with 10 ml rice vinegar and pinch salt; prepare 100 g kimchi; chop 10 g scallions; warm 4 large whole-wheat tortillas.\n\n**Ingredients**\n- 400 g beef sirloin, 25 ml low-sodium soy sauce, 6 g honey or grated pear, 10 ml sesame oil, ginger, garlic, 5 ml rice vinegar, 5 ml gochujang.\n- 200 g brown rice, 4 eggs, 30 ml milk, 100 g kimchi, 1 cucumber, 10 ml rice vinegar, 10 g scallions, 4 whole-wheat tortillas, sesame seeds.\n\n**Method**\n1. Cook bulgogi: Heat a skillet until hot. Sear marinated beef in batches for 2 min until caramelised; the honey/pear in the marinade will help develop a glaze. Set aside.\n2. Scramble eggs: In the same pan, add a knob of butter and cook beaten eggs gently until just set; season.\n3. Assemble burritos: Lay tortillas on a board. Divide rice down the centre of each, top with bulgogi, scrambled eggs, kimchi, cucumber pickles and scallions. Sprinkle with sesame seeds and extra gochujang if desired.\n4. Roll & sear: Fold sides in and roll tightly. Sear seam-side down in a hot dry pan for 1 min to seal.\n\n**Why this works**\nMarinating thinly sliced beef with soy, sugar and gochujang tenderises the meat and builds caramelisation. Whole-wheat tortillas and brown rice provide fibre. Incorporating kimchi and pickled cucumber adds fermentation acids to balance the rich beef and eggs. Compliance refinement: pear or a small amount of honey supports caramelisation while keeping added sugar low; low-sodium soy lowers salt load.\n\n**Plating / Pairing**\nServe halved burritos with a side of sliced avocado. Pair with a lightly sweet cold brew tea or a session ale.\n\n**DGA Compliance Review**\nReviewed against the embedded DGA rule set. Recipe keeps its original flavor-map role while using whole/minimally processed ingredients, whole grains where applicable, controlled added sugar, protein diversity, and low-additive technique choices.\n- Reduced added sweetener to 6 g total or replaced with grated pear.\n- Changed soy sauce to low-sodium.",
