      "plating": "Cut into squares and serve with espresso. Pair with an almond-milk cortado or unsweetened espresso; Vin Santo is an optional adult pairing only.",
      "fullMarkdown": "## Lucuma Tiramisu (Italian × Peruvian)\n**Servings: 4 | Active time: 45 min | Total time: 4 h (includes chilling)**\n\n**Mise en place**\n- **Station A - Ladyfingers:** Prepare a batter with 3 eggs (separated), 20 g raw sugar, 75 g whole-wheat pastry flour and 5 g baking powder. Pipe onto parchment and bake at 180 °C for 10 min until just set.\n- **Station B - Lucuma cream:** Whisk 3 egg yolks with 20 g honey over a bain-marie until pale. Beat in 250 g mascarpone and 150 g lucuma purée until smooth.\n- **Station C - Espresso soak:** Brew 200 ml strong espresso; stir in 5 ml almond extract. Marsala is optional for adult service only.\n\n**Ingredients**\n- **Ladyfingers:** 3 eggs, 20 g raw sugar, 75 g whole-wheat pastry flour, 5 g baking powder.\n- **Lucuma cream:** 3 egg yolks, 20 g honey, 250 g mascarpone, 150 g lucuma purée, pinch salt.\n- **Espresso soak:** 200 ml espresso, 5 ml almond extract or 20 ml Marsala only as optional adult variation.\n- **Topping:** 30 g unsweetened dark cocoa powder, 20 g shaved 85% dark chocolate.\n\n**Method**\n1. Bake ladyfingers: Beat egg whites to stiff peaks; gradually add the 20 g sugar. In another bowl, beat yolks with no additional sugar until pale. Fold in flour and baking powder, then fold in meringue. Pipe into fingers and bake until lightly golden. Cool.\n2. Make lucuma cream: Cook yolks and 20 g honey over a gentle bain-marie until thick ribbons form. Cool slightly, then fold in mascarpone and lucuma purée until smooth.\n3. Assemble tiramisu: Dip ladyfingers briefly into cooled espresso soak and arrange a single layer in a glass dish. Spread half the lucuma cream over. Repeat with another layer. Smooth the top and chill at least 3 h.\n4. Finish: Dust with cocoa powder and garnish with shaved dark chocolate just before serving.\n\n**Why this works**\nWhole-wheat ladyfingers stay light because whipped egg whites provide structure and lift, while lucuma contributes caramel-like natural sweetness. The revised formula limits added sugar to 40 g total, or 10 g per serving, and keeps Marsala optional rather than default.\n\n**Plating / Pairing**\nCut into squares and serve with espresso. Pair with an almond-milk cortado or unsweetened espresso; Vin Santo is an optional adult pairing only.\n\n**DGA Compliance Review**\nReviewed against the embedded DGA rule set. Recipe keeps its original flavor-map role while using whole/minimally processed ingredients, whole grains where applicable, controlled added sugar, protein diversity, and low-additive technique choices.\n- Reduced total added sugar to 40 g for 4 servings.\n- Made Marsala optional and almond extract the default.\n- Specified unsweetened cocoa and 85% chocolate.",
