      "plating": "Serve as a pre-meal snack with sparkling wine or a chilled lager.",
      "fullMarkdown": "## Parmesan-Reggiano Crisps with Aji Amarillo Aioli (Italian × Peruvian)\n**Servings: 4 (snack) | Active time: 15 min | Total time: 30 min**\n\n**Mise en place**\n- Station A - Crisps: Finely grate 100 g Parmigiano-Reggiano and 50 g aged cheddar; line a baking tray with silicone.\n- Station B - Aioli: Separate 1 egg yolk; measure 5 ml lemon juice, 5 ml white vinegar, 5 g Dijon mustard, 50 g aji amarillo paste and 100 ml olive oil. Mince 1 garlic clove.\n\n**Ingredients**\n- Crisps: 100 g Parmigiano-Reggiano, 50 g aged cheddar, 2 g smoked paprika.\n- Aji aioli: 1 egg yolk, 5 ml lemon juice, 5 ml white vinegar, 5 g Dijon mustard, 50 g aji amarillo paste, 100 ml olive oil, 1 minced garlic clove, salt.\n\n**Method**\n1. Bake crisps: Preheat oven to 200 °C. On a silicone-lined sheet, spoon 15 g mounds of cheese mixture, leaving space to spread. Flatten gently and sprinkle with smoked paprika. Bake for 6-8 min until golden and lace-like. Cool completely to crisp.\n2. Make aioli: In a bowl, whisk egg yolk, lemon juice, vinegar and mustard. Slowly drizzle in olive oil while whisking until thick and emulsified. Stir in aji amarillo paste and minced garlic; season.\n3. Serve: Plate crisps with a bowl of aioli for dipping.\n\n**Why this works**\nParmesan’s low moisture content melts into lacy crisps that firm up upon cooling. Adding cheddar provides additional sharpness. Making aioli from scratch allows control over oil and eliminates additives; aji amarillo brings floral heat and golden hue.\n\n**Plating / Pairing**\nServe as a pre-meal snack with sparkling wine or a chilled lager.\n\n**DGA Compliance Review**\nReviewed against the embedded DGA rule set. Recipe keeps its original flavor-map role while using whole/minimally processed ingredients, whole grains where applicable, controlled added sugar, protein diversity, and low-additive technique choices.\n- Added DGA compliance metadata and sodium/additive-aware execution notes where relevant.",
