      "fullMarkdown": "## Roasted Plantain Chips with Rocoto Dip (Peruvian)\n**Servings: 4 | Active time: 15 min | Total time: 40 min**\n\n**Mise en place**\n- Station A - Plantains: Peel 3 green plantains and slice thinly on a mandolin; soak in salted water for 10 min.\n- Station B - Seasoning: Mix 20 ml olive oil with 5 g cumin, 5 g smoked paprika and 5 g salt.\n- Station C - Rocoto dip: Blend 1 roasted red pepper, 1 fresh rocoto chile (seeded), 1 garlic clove, 50 g Greek yoghurt, 20 ml olive oil, 10 ml lime juice and salt.\n\n**Ingredients**\n- 3 green plantains, 20 ml olive oil, 5 g cumin, 5 g smoked paprika, 5 g salt.\n- Dip: 1 roasted red pepper, 1 rocoto chile, 1 garlic clove, 50 g Greek yoghurt, 20 ml olive oil, 10 ml lime juice, salt.\n\n**Method**\n1. Prepare chips: Drain plantain slices and pat dry. Toss with spiced oil. Arrange in a single layer on a lined baking sheet. Roast at 200 °C for 20-25 min, flipping halfway, until crisp and golden.\n2. Make dip: Blend roasted pepper, rocoto, garlic, yoghurt, olive oil and lime juice until smooth. Season with salt.\n3. Serve: Serve warm plantain chips with rocoto dip.\n\n**Why this works**\nSoaking plantains removes excess starch, promoting crispness. Roasting with a thin coating of oil yields chips with a satisfying crunch without deep frying. Rocoto provides fruity heat balanced by creamy yoghurt.\n\n**Plating / Pairing**\nServe in a parchment-lined basket with dip on the side. Pair with a pilsner or passion fruit iced tea.\n\n**DGA Compliance Review**\nReviewed against the embedded DGA rule set. Recipe keeps its original flavor-map role while using whole/minimally processed ingredients, whole grains where applicable, controlled added sugar, protein diversity, and low-additive technique choices.\n- Added DGA compliance metadata and sodium/additive-aware execution notes where relevant.",
