      "fullMarkdown": "## Slow-Roasted Salmon & Avocado Whole-Grain Bagel (American × Peruvian)\n**Servings: 4 | Active time: 30 min | Total time: 3 h (includes proofing)**\n\n**Mise en place**\n- **Station A - Bagels:** Mix dough with 250 g whole-wheat flour, 250 g bread flour, 7 g yeast, 6 g barley malt syrup, 300 ml warm water, 10 g salt. Knead and proof 1 h; shape into rings and proof again. Prepare water bath with 20 g baking soda.\n- **Station B - Salmon:** Season 400 g salmon fillet with 8 g salt, orange zest, black pepper, dill, and 10 ml olive oil. Roast at 95 °C until just opaque and silky, then chill and flake or slice.\n- **Station C - Toppings:** Slice 2 avocados thinly, pickle 1 red onion in 30 ml cider vinegar with 4 g honey, chop fresh dill, mix 200 g cream cheese with 10 g chopped chives.\n\n**Ingredients**\n- **Bagels:** 250 g whole-wheat flour, 250 g bread flour, 7 g yeast, 6 g malt syrup, 300 ml water, 10 g salt, 20 g baking soda for boiling.\n- **Slow-roasted salmon:** 400 g salmon fillet, 8 g salt, zest of 1 orange, black pepper, fresh dill, 10 ml olive oil.\n- **Toppings:** 2 avocados, 1 red onion, 30 ml cider vinegar, 4 g honey, 200 g cream cheese, 10 g chives, fresh dill, lemon wedges.\n\n**Method**\n1. **Make bagels:** After second proof, boil bagels in alkaline water for 30 s per side; sprinkle with sesame seeds if desired; bake at 220 °C for 15 min until golden.\n2. **Roast salmon:** Season salmon with salt, orange zest, pepper, dill, and olive oil. Roast at 95 °C until the thickest part reaches 50-52 °C, about 20-25 min. Chill slightly, then flake or slice.\n3. **Assemble:** Split bagels and spread with chive cream cheese. Layer with avocado slices, slow-roasted salmon and lightly pickled red onions. Sprinkle with dill and serve with lemon wedges.\n\n**Why this works**\nBoiling bagels in an alkaline bath gelatinises exterior starch for the signature shiny chew, while whole-wheat flour adds fiber. Slow-roasting fresh salmon avoids a salt-and-sweet cure, keeps the texture buttery, and preserves the seafood-forward flavor-map cue with less sodium than commercial smoked salmon.\n\n**Plating / Pairing**\nServe open-faced or closed with dressed greens. Pair with citrus-infused sparkling water or a crisp rosé as an optional adult pairing.\n\n**DGA Compliance Review**\nReviewed against the embedded DGA rule set. Recipe keeps its original flavor-map role while using whole/minimally processed ingredients, whole grains where applicable, controlled added sugar, protein diversity, and low-additive technique choices.\n- Replaced commercially cured salmon with fresh slow-roasted salmon.\n- Reduced malt syrup to 6 g and pickle sweetener to 4 g.",
