      "fullMarkdown": "## Spaghetti Cacio e Pepe Oatmeal (Italian × Andean)\n**Servings: 4 | Active time: 15 min | Total time: 25 min**\n\n**Mise en place**\n- Station A - Oats: Measure 200 g rolled oats and 600 ml water. Grate 80 g Pecorino Romano and 20 g Parmigiano-Reggiano. Grind 5 g black pepper.\n- Station B - Mushrooms: Clean and slice 200 g porcini or mixed mushrooms; mince 1 garlic clove; pick fresh thyme.\n- Station C - Eggs (optional): Poach or fry 4 eggs for topping.\n\n**Ingredients**\n- 200 g rolled oats, 600 ml water, 200 ml whole milk, 80 g Pecorino Romano, 20 g Parmigiano-Reggiano, 5 g freshly ground black pepper, 20 ml olive oil, 200 g mushrooms, 1 garlic clove, fresh thyme, salt.\n\n**Method**\n1. Cook mushrooms: Sauté mushrooms in olive oil until golden; add minced garlic and thyme; season.\n2. Make oatmeal: In a saucepan, bring water and milk to a boil. Stir in oats; cook 5 min until creamy. Stir in cheeses and black pepper vigorously to emulsify. Adjust thickness with additional milk.\n3. Serve: Spoon oatmeal into bowls; top with sautéed mushrooms and an optional poached or fried egg. Grind extra pepper on top.\n\n**Why this works**\nOats absorb liquid quickly, and adding cheese off heat prevents curdling. Freshly ground pepper releases volatile compounds that define this classic Roman flavour. Mushrooms add umami and meaty texture.\n\n**Plating / Pairing**\nServe immediately while hot. Pair with a macchiato or a lightly floral white wine.\n\n**DGA Compliance Review**\nReviewed against the embedded DGA rule set. Recipe keeps its original flavor-map role while using whole/minimally processed ingredients, whole grains where applicable, controlled added sugar, protein diversity, and low-additive technique choices.\n- Added DGA compliance metadata and sodium/additive-aware execution notes where relevant.",
