      "plating": "Serve with arugula and orange segments. Pair with cappuccino, black coffee, or sparkling orange water.",
      "fullMarkdown": "## Whole-Grain Croissant with Roast Turkey & Queso Fresco (French × Peruvian)\n**Servings: 4 | Active time: 1 h | Total time: 12 h (includes laminating/proofing)**\n\n**Mise en place**\n- **Station A - Dough:** Prepare détrempe: combine 200 g whole-wheat flour, 200 g bread flour, 10 g yeast, 16 g raw sugar, 8 g salt, 220 ml cold milk and 50 g melted butter. Knead and refrigerate.\n- **Station B - Butter block:** Flatten 250 g cold butter between parchment to a 20 cm square. Chill.\n- **Station C - Filling:** Slice 200 g home-roasted turkey breast or pork tenderloin and 200 g queso fresco; prepare 50 g rocoto-orange glaze with 20 g honey, orange zest and vinegar.\n\n**Ingredients**\n- 200 g whole-wheat flour, 200 g bread flour, 10 g instant yeast, 16 g raw sugar, 8 g salt, 220 ml milk, 50 g butter, 250 g butter for laminating.\n- Filling: 200 g home-roasted turkey breast or pork tenderloin, 200 g queso fresco, 50 g rocoto-orange glaze made from roasted rocoto, orange zest, 20 g honey, and 10 ml vinegar.\n\n**Method**\n1. **Laminate dough:** Encapsulate butter block within détrempe and perform three single folds, resting dough in the refrigerator between folds to keep butter cold. Roll to 0.5 cm thick, cut into triangles and shape into croissants. Proof 2 h until puffy.\n2. **Bake:** Brush with egg wash and bake at 200 °C for 15 min until deeply golden and flaky.\n3. **Assemble:** Split croissants; spread a thin layer of rocoto-orange glaze. Fill with home-roasted turkey or pork tenderloin and queso fresco. Serve warm.\n\n**Why this works**\nWhole-wheat flour is tempered with bread flour to preserve flakiness while increasing fiber. Cold butter layers create steam for distinct lamination. The revision removes processed cured deli meat and keeps added sugar below 10 g per serving by lowering dough sugar and using a small honey-based glaze.\n\n**Plating / Pairing**\nServe with arugula and orange segments. Pair with cappuccino, black coffee, or sparkling orange water.\n\n**DGA Compliance Review**\nReviewed against the embedded DGA rule set. Recipe keeps its original flavor-map role while using whole/minimally processed ingredients, whole grains where applicable, controlled added sugar, protein diversity, and low-additive technique choices.\n- Replaced cured deli meat/cured deli meat with home-roasted turkey or pork tenderloin.\n- Reduced dough sugar and glaze sweetener to keep added sugar under 10 g/serving.",
