      "plating": "Slice and serve immediately with arugula or radicchio. Pair with sparkling water, bitter orange soda with no added sugar, or dry Lambrusco as optional adult service.",
      "fullMarkdown": "## Whole-Grain Pizza Diavola with Spicy Mushrooms & Rocoto Honey (Italian × Peruvian)\n**Servings: 4 | Active time: 45 min | Total time: 18 h (includes dough fermentation)**\n\n**Mise en place**\n- **Station A - Dough:** Combine 250 g whole-wheat flour, 250 g bread flour, 2 g instant yeast, 350 ml water, 10 g salt and 20 ml olive oil. Refrigerate 12-24 h; bring to room temperature 2 h before baking.\n- **Station B - Sauce & toppings:** Simmer 400 g crushed tomatoes with garlic and oregano. Roast mushrooms and cherry tomatoes with olive oil, chili flakes and salt until deeply browned. Slice bell pepper, red onion and mozzarella.\n- **Station C - Rocoto honey:** Warm 24 g honey with 20 g rocoto paste; cool.\n\n**Ingredients**\n- 250 g whole-wheat flour, 250 g bread flour, 2 g yeast, 350 ml water, 10 g salt, 20 ml olive oil.\n- Toppings: 400 g crushed tomatoes with no added sugar, 2 garlic cloves, oregano, 250 g oyster or cremini mushrooms, 120 g cherry tomatoes, 1 red bell pepper, 1 red onion, 200 g mozzarella, 24 g rocoto honey, 10 g chili flakes, 15 ml olive oil.\n\n**Method**\n1. **Prepare dough:** Mix and knead gently. Refrigerate 12-24 h. On baking day, divide, shape into balls and rest until puffy.\n2. **Preheat oven:** Heat a baking stone at 250 °C for at least 45 min. Stretch dough into 30 cm rounds.\n3. **Assemble pizza:** Spread a thin layer of tomato sauce. Top with roasted mushrooms, cherry tomatoes, bell pepper, onion and mozzarella. Bake on the stone for 8-10 min until crust is crisp and toppings are bubbling.\n4. **Finish:** Drizzle with a measured 24 g rocoto honey and sprinkle with chili flakes and fresh oregano.\n\n**Why this works**\nLong fermentation builds flavor and extensibility in the whole-grain dough. Roasted mushrooms and tomatoes replace processed deli meat with Maillard-rich umami, preserving the Diavola mood without processed meat. Rocoto honey is portioned at 24 g total, or 6 g added sugar per serving.\n\n**Plating / Pairing**\nSlice and serve immediately with arugula or radicchio. Pair with sparkling water, bitter orange soda with no added sugar, or dry Lambrusco as optional adult service.\n\n**DGA Compliance Review**\nReviewed against the embedded DGA rule set. Recipe keeps its original flavor-map role while using whole/minimally processed ingredients, whole grains where applicable, controlled added sugar, protein diversity, and low-additive technique choices.\n- Removed processed deli meat entirely.\n- Reduced rocoto honey to 24 g total.\n- Kept Diavola heat through mushrooms, chile, and rocoto.",
