      "plating": "Use for slow-roasted salmon bagels, egg sandwiches, or avocado toast. Pair with black coffee or sparkling citrus water.",
      "fullMarkdown": "## Whole-Grain Bagels (Base recipe / whole-grain bakery)\n**Servings: 8 bagels | Active time: 45 min | Total time: 3 h**\n\n**Mise en place**\n- Mix 250 g whole-wheat flour, 250 g bread flour, 7 g yeast, 6 g barley malt syrup, 300 ml warm water, and 10 g salt.\n- Prepare a baking tray with parchment and a wide pot with water plus 20 g baking soda.\n- Set aside sesame, poppy, or everything-style seed mix with no additives.\n\n**Ingredients**\n- 250 g whole-wheat flour\n- 250 g bread flour\n- 7 g instant yeast\n- 6 g barley malt syrup\n- 300 ml warm water\n- 10 g salt\n- 20 g baking soda for boiling water\n- Optional: 20 g sesame or poppy seeds\n\n**Method**\n1. Knead the dough 8-10 min until elastic. Cover and proof 1 h, or until visibly puffy.\n2. Divide into 8 pieces, shape into rings, and rest 20-30 min.\n3. Boil each bagel in the baking-soda water for 30 s per side.\n4. Bake at 220 °C for 15-18 min until deeply golden and shiny.\n5. Cool at least 15 min before slicing to preserve the chewy crumb.\n\n**Why this works**\nWhole-wheat flour adds fiber and nutty flavor; bread flour preserves the chew associated with bagels. The alkaline boil gelatinizes surface starch so the crust bakes glossy and resilient. Only 6 g malt syrup is used across the entire batch, keeping added sugar very low per serving.\n\n**Plating / Pairing**\nUse for slow-roasted salmon bagels, egg sandwiches, or avocado toast. Pair with black coffee or sparkling citrus water.\n\n**DGA Compliance Review**\nReviewed against the embedded DGA rule set. Recipe keeps its original flavor-map role while using whole/minimally processed ingredients, whole grains where applicable, controlled added sugar, protein diversity, and low-additive technique choices.\n- Updated base note to reflect lower malt syrup and fresh salmon service.",
